/*
================================================================================
Detection ID:       DET-001
Title:              Network Service Scanning (Port Sweep)
MITRE ATT&CK:       T1046 - Network Service Scanning
Data Source:        Sysmon Event ID 3 (Network Connection)
Severity:           Medium
Author:             Idris Lawan Mustapha
Target Platform:    Splunk Cloud Platform
================================================================================
Description:
Identifies anomalous network connections where a single external or internal 
source IP connects to an unusually high number of unique destination ports on 
a target host within a short time window. Typical of automated port scanners 
(Nmap, Masscan, Zenmap).

False Positives:
- Authorized internal vulnerability scanners (Nessus, Qualys, Rapid7 InsightVM)
- Network performance monitoring agents and asset discovery tools
Mitigation / Tuning: Whitelist authorized scanner IP ranges using a lookup table:
`NOT [| inputlookup authorized_scanners.csv | fields src_ip]`
================================================================================
*/

// Standard Extracted Field Query:
index=main EventCode=3
| stats dc(DestinationPort) as unique_ports count by src_ip
| where unique_ports > 20
| sort -unique_ports

// Sysmon XmlWinEventLog Fallback / Direct PCRE Extraction Query:
// Used when Sysmon events are ingested with renderXml=true before XML field extraction
index=main sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" "<EventID>3</EventID>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='SourceIp'>(?<src_ip>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='DestinationPort'>(?<dest_port>[^<]+)</Data>"
| stats dc(dest_port) as unique_ports count by src_ip
| where unique_ports > 1
| sort -unique_ports
